      "body": "Magnitude is pure Pythagoras: |⟨a, b⟩| = √(a² + b²). The components are the legs of a right triangle; the vector is the hypotenuse. That's why ⟨3, 4⟩, ⟨5, 12⟩, and ⟨6, 8⟩ have the clean lengths 5, 13, and 10 — they're the Pythagorean triples.",
      "figure": "vec-magnitude"
    },
